    "q-33095": {
      "dom_id": "step-q33095",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "${(\\frac{1}{3}+{x}^{2})}^{2}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the following formula:\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{2}={a}^{2}+2ab+{b}^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=\\frac{1}{3}$ and $b={x}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{1}{3}+{x}^{2})}^{2} & = \\\\ {(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}+2(\\frac{1}{3})({x}^{2})+{({x}^{2})}^{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{2}+{x}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
